  "notes": "Godan verb (す row): {寝過|ねす}ごす・{寝過|ねす}ごします\nて-form: {寝過|ねす}ごして\nた-form: {寝過|ねす}ごした\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- うっかり{寝過|ねす}ごす (to accidentally oversleep)\n- {寝過|ねす}ごして{遅刻|ちこく}する (to oversleep and be late)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {寝坊|ねぼう}する: Also means to oversleep, but is more commonly used in everyday conversation. {寝過|ねす}ごす emphasizes sleeping past a specific point, while {寝坊|ねぼう}する simply means getting up late.\n- {乗|の}り{過|す}ごす: To ride past one's stop — uses the same ～{過|す}ごす pattern.",
